From: Anonymous
Subject: [PATCH] drm/amd/display: HDMI 2.1 PCON support on DCN201 (amdgpu.bc250_hdmi21)

Advertise dc->caps.dp_hdmi21_pcon_support on DCN201, behind a BC-250
module parameter, amdgpu.bc250_hdmi21, that defaults to on and exists
so that amdgpu.bc250_hdmi21=0 gives an unpatched kernel back.

DCN201 is the only DCN2-class resource pool that leaves that flag false.
What it gates is which ceiling link_validation.c checks a mode against
through a DP-to-HDMI converter: with it set, the converter's FRL link
bandwidth read from DPCD; without it, the converter's TMDS pixel-clock
limit (one DPCD byte times 2.5 MHz, 600 MHz in practice). Against 600
MHz, 4K120 is reachable only at 4:2:0 8-bit and 4K60 HDR only via 4:2:2,
whatever the adapter's own HDMI side can do.

The parameter is plumbed the way DC expects OS-side switches to arrive:
amdgpu_drv.c defines it, amdgpu_dm.c copies it into dc_init_data.flags,
and it lands in dc->config.bc250_hdmi21, which the resource pool reads.
With amdgpu.bc250_hdmi21=0 every touched path is identical to an
unpatched kernel.

Author: TeleBooth, published at
https://gist.github.com/TeleBooth/d88ef745895d444a401d0e621de9818e
as bc250-dcn201-pcon-hdmi21.patch (the file itself is signed "Anonymous").
Tested by them and several other BC-250 owners at 3840x2160@120Hz 4:4:4
through a Cable Matters 102101 PCON into an LG CX, and on an LG G5
through a UGREEN 8K adapter with this exact patch (4K120 RGB, DSC 12 bpp
over HBR2 x4, FRL PCON negotiated). Verified on hardware; the parameter
stays as the off switch for anyone who wants an unpatched kernel back.
Reproduced blackouts with it off proved DSC was never the cause.

Carried here until it lands upstream.
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu.h b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu.h
index 0dd8e2375c4d..22b043235045 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu.h
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu.h
@@ -259,6 +259,7 @@ extern int amdgpu_num_kcq;
 #define AMDGPU_UMSCHFW_LOG_SIZE (32 * 1024)
 extern int amdgpu_vcnfw_log;
 extern int amdgpu_sg_display;
+extern int amdgpu_bc250_hdmi21;
 extern int amdgpu_umsch_mm;
 extern int amdgpu_seamless;
 extern int amdgpu_umsch_mm_fwlog;
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_drv.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_drv.c
index b72058e1a3d8..9fe6d55119c0 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_drv.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_drv.c
@@ -236,6 +236,7 @@ int amdgpu_smartshift_bias;
 int amdgpu_use_xgmi_p2p = 1;
 int amdgpu_vcnfw_log;
 int amdgpu_sg_display = -1; /* auto */
+int amdgpu_bc250_hdmi21 = 1;
 int amdgpu_user_partt_mode = AMDGPU_AUTO_COMPUTE_PARTITION_MODE;
 int amdgpu_umsch_mm;
 int amdgpu_seamless = -1; /* auto */
@@ -985,6 +986,17 @@ module_param_named(vcnfw_log, amdgpu_vcnfw_log, int, 0444);
 MODULE_PARM_DESC(sg_display, "S/G Display (-1 = auto (default), 0 = disable)");
 module_param_named(sg_display, amdgpu_sg_display, int, 0444);
 
+/**
+ * DOC: bc250_hdmi21 (int)
+ * BC-250 (Cyan Skillfish, DCN 2.0.1) only. Enable HDMI 2.1 PCON negotiation
+ * and the two on-die DSC engines, both of which the DCN201 driver otherwise
+ * leaves disabled. Needed for 4K120 at 4:4:4 through a DP 1.4 to HDMI 2.1
+ * FRL adapter; inert on a native DisplayPort monitor or a passive adapter.
+ * (0 = disabled, 1 = enabled (default))
+ */
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(bc250_hdmi21, "BC-250: HDMI 2.1 PCON and DSC on DCN201 (0 = disabled, 1 = enabled (default))");
+module_param_named(bc250_hdmi21, amdgpu_bc250_hdmi21, int, 0444);
+
 /**
  * DOC: umsch_mm (int)
  * Enable Multi Media User Mode Scheduler. This is a HW scheduling engine for VCN and VPE.
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm.c
index 36982ca89d1f..26c844557770 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm.c
@@ -2147,6 +2147,8 @@ static int amdgpu_dm_init(struct amdgpu_device *adev)
 	if (amdgpu_dc_feature_mask & DC_FRL_MASK)
 		init_data.flags.enable_frl = true;
 
+	init_data.flags.bc250_hdmi21 = (amdgpu_bc250_hdmi21 != 0);
+
 	init_data.flags.seamless_boot_edp_requested = false;
 
 	if (amdgpu_device_seamless_boot_supported(adev)) {
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/dc/dc.h b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/dc/dc.h
index dfe41d46b3f1..b9571ba0e921 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/dc/dc.h
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/dc/dc.h
@@ -590,6 +590,7 @@ struct dc_config {
 	bool ignore_dpref_ss;
 	bool enable_mipi_converter_optimization;
 	bool enable_frl;
+	bool bc250_hdmi21;
 	bool force_hdmi21_frl_enc_enable;
 	bool skip_frl_pretraining;
 	bool use_default_clock_table;
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/dc/resource/dcn201/dcn201_resource.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/dc/resource/dcn201/dcn201_resource.c
index 02b7dc07ad53..e2819852a40a 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/dc/resource/dcn201/dcn201_resource.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/dc/resource/dcn201/dcn201_resource.c
@@ -1331,6 +1331,10 @@ static bool dcn201_resource_construct(
 
 	dc->caps.max_odm_combine_factor = 2;
 
+	/* BC-250: amdgpu.bc250_hdmi21, on by default; 0 restores stock behaviour */
+	if (dc->config.bc250_hdmi21)
+		dc->caps.dp_hdmi21_pcon_support = true;
+
 	dc->cap_funcs = cap_funcs;
 
 	return true;
